WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.847 --> 00:00:02.937
In the moulding shop stands a press.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:06.959
The cover for the filling unit of line 3 comes out of it.

3
00:00:07.994 --> 00:00:11.732
An injection moulding machine makes plastic parts by injecting

4
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.343
molten plastic into a steel mould and letting it set.

5
00:00:16.398 --> 00:00:17.989
Six topics follow the cover.

6
00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:21.588
The machine, the cycle and the plastics make it.

7
00:00:22.646 --> 00:00:26.744
Defects, process setting and moulds make sure every cover is good.

8
00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.753
The first topic is The machine.

9
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.684
The injection unit melts the plastic and the clamp unit holds the mould.

10
00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:38.704
The clamp force keeps the mould shut against the pressure.

11
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.230
Too little gives flash on the cover.

12
00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:44.583
For the machine we look at the tie bars.

13
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.091
The mould has to fit between them.

14
00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:50.801
The second topic is Cycle and output.

15
00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:54.976
A cycle runs from one closing of the mould to the next.

16
00:00:55.996 --> 00:00:58.074
The cooling usually takes longest.

17
00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.453
So it decides how many covers you make per hour.

18
00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:06.901
For cooling we often use cooling channels and a temperature control unit.

19
00:01:08.264 --> 00:01:10.063
The third topic is Plastics.

20
00:01:10.778 --> 00:01:12.856
The granules are thermoplastics.

21
00:01:13.552 --> 00:01:16.246
They melt when heated and set again when cooled.

22
00:01:17.294 --> 00:01:20.521
The cover is polycarbonate, clear and hard to break.

23
00:01:21.232 --> 00:01:23.217
But it absorbs water from the air.

24
00:01:24.223 --> 00:01:27.567
So with plastics we often use a dryer for the granules.

25
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:30.652
The fourth topic is Defects.

26
00:01:31.381 --> 00:01:34.098
On a cover you can see flash or a sink mark.

27
00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.615
Flash is plastic where it should not be.

28
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.816
A sink mark is a dent above a thick section.

29
00:01:41.859 --> 00:01:44.506
For defects we compare with a boundary sample.

30
00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.182
So every shift judges the same.

31
00:01:48.464 --> 00:01:50.380
The fifth topic is Process setting.

32
00:01:51.145 --> 00:01:54.407
On the screen, five groups of settings decide the part.

33
00:01:55.531 --> 00:01:56.704
They affect each other.

34
00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:59.785
So the setter does not just turn one of them.

35
00:02:00.782 --> 00:02:04.671
For setting we start with the setting sheet for this mould on this press.

36
00:02:05.953 --> 00:02:07.741
The sixth topic is Moulds.

37
00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:11.699
The mould is the costly part, made for this cover only.

38
00:02:12.745 --> 00:02:15.067
You service the mould before it breaks.

39
00:02:15.778 --> 00:02:18.262
Otherwise you get flash on the cover later.

40
00:02:19.243 --> 00:02:22.378
For moulds we often use a hot runner and a shot counter,

41
00:02:22.494 --> 00:02:24.572
which counts how often it closes.

42
00:02:25.565 --> 00:02:26.517
The cover is good.

43
00:02:27.278 --> 00:02:30.598
It goes to the filling unit of line 3 in hall B.

44
00:02:31.887 --> 00:02:33.071
This is the whole map.

45
00:02:33.803 --> 00:02:37.391
Injection moulding is the sixth station of Making things.

46
00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.105
Every topic has four levels.

47
00:02:41.084 --> 00:02:43.464
Start with The machine, at Basics level.

48
00:02:44.155 --> 00:02:47.441
That first lesson shows one whole cycle of the press.

49
00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.932
At Working knowledge level come the screw, the cooling and the plastic families.

50
00:02:53.652 --> 00:02:55.382
You look for the cause of a defect,

51
00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.343
set the process window and look inside the mould.

52
00:02:59.416 --> 00:03:01.819
At Advanced level you choose the right press,

53
00:03:01.993 --> 00:03:04.280
weigh more cavities and tackle warpage.

54
00:03:05.058 --> 00:03:07.961
Then come three studies and the mould maintenance.

55
00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:13.508
At Expert level you know all kinds of presses and work out the part cost.

56
00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:16.720
You work with glass fibre and recyclate,

57
00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.832
solve defects for good and validate the process.

58
00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.904
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
